      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Neversink River, flowing through Claryville, is celebrated as the birthplace of American fly fishing.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neversink%2C_New_York",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "When the Neversink Reservoir was completed in 1953, the original town was moved a couple of miles, making its name ironic.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neversink%2C_New_York",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Claryville lies within the Catskill Park, offering scenic trails and wildlife for outdoor enthusiasts.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neversink%2C_New_York",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "A 1941 decision by New York City’s water board selected the Claryville area as a reservoir site to supply the city’s growing water needs.",
